      },
      "displayName": "Aaron Birkland",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "There is another issue related to DC field length: ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "http://fedora-commons.org/jira/browse/FCREPO-682"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "http://fedora-commons.org/jira/browse/FCREPO-682",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Depending on the choice of database, the field search impl may will the same problem with long DC fields (but won't leave the RI in an inconsistent state).   Mysql will silently truncate the index entry, PostgresQL will throw an exception if the value is too large to index. ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
